<title>UK: BASKETBALL-EUROLEAGUE COLLATED RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BASKETBALL-EUROLEAGUE COLLATED RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results of men's EuroLeague basketball matches on Thursday:</p>
<p>Group E</p>
<p>In Moscow:</p>
<p>CSKA Moscow (Russia)  70  Olympiakos (Greece) 79  (halftime 30-41)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Olympiakos - Dragan Tarlac 20</p>
<p>CSKA Moscow - Sergei Bazarevich 20</p>
<p>In Milan:</p>
<p>Stefanel Milan (Italy) 73 Charleroi (Belgium) 63  (38-27)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Stefanel - Gregor Fucka 21, Alessandro Del Pol 14, Anthony Bowie 10</p>
<p>Charleroi - Eric Cleymans 15, Ron Ellis 11, David Desy 10</p>
<p>Attendance: 2,500</p>
<p>In Tel Aviv:</p>
<p>Maccabi Tel Aviv (Israel) 78 Alba Berlin (Germany) 62 (37-26)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Maccabi Tel Aviv - Randy White 25, Nadav Henefeld 16, Doron Sheffer 14.</p>
<p>Alba Berlin - Wendel Alexis 16, Sasha Obradovic 15, Henrik Rudl 12.</p>
<p>Group F</p>
<p>In Madrid:</p>
<p>Estudiantes (Spain) 68 Limoges (France) 70 (38-29)</p>
<p>In Zagreb:</p>
<p>Cibona Zagreb (Croatia)  82 Ulker Spor (Turkey)  81 (In overtime. Halftime 37-26. At normal time 70-70)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Cibona: Slaven Rimac 22, Zdravko Radulovic 16, Damir Mulaomerovic 11.</p>
<p>Ulker: Ene 31, Godfrid 10, Erdenai 10.</p>
<p>Attendance: 6,000.</p>
<p>Group G</p>
<p>In Ljubljana:</p>
<p>    Sevilla (Spain)	70  Ljubljana (Slovenia) 67</p>
<p>(35-40)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Ljubljana - Radko Nesterovic 19</p>
<p>Seville - Tellis Frank 22</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,000</p>
<p>In Athens:</p>
<p>Panathinaikos (Greece) 71  Dynamo Moscow (Russia) 67 (33-38)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Panathinaikos - Frangiskos Alvertis 20, Byron Dinkins 15, Nikos Economou 10</p>
<p>Dynamo - Mikael Soloviev 16, Ruslan Boitakov 15, Vitaly Nosov 14 Prosports exrome. here hoops result:</p>
<p>Group H</p>
<p>In Salonika:</p>
<p>Partizan Belgrade (Yugoslavia) 71  Split (Croatia) 82</p>
<p>In Bologna:</p>
<p>Kinder Bologna (Italy) 92 Barcelona (Spain) 103 (51-40)</p>
<p>Leading scorers:</p>
<p>Kinder - Komazec 39, Savic 22</p>
<p>Barcelona - Fernandez 23, Djordjevic 15</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,650</p>
